 # Task API

 A small in-memory CRUD API built with Express. It manages tasks with an `id`,
 `title`, and `done` status. Data is stored in memory and is reset whenever the
 server restarts.

 ## Install and run

 From this directory, run:

 ```bash
 npm install && node index.js
 ```

 The API runs at `http://localhost:3000`.

 Interactive Swagger documentation is available at:

 `http://localhost:3000/docs/`

 ## Endpoints

 | Method | Endpoint | Description | Body |
 | --- | --- | --- | --- |
 | GET | `/` | Get API information | None |
 | GET | `/health` | Check API health | None |
 | GET | `/tasks` | Get all tasks | None |
 | POST | `/tasks` | Create a task | `{ "title": "Buy milk" }` |
 | GET | `/tasks/:id` | Get one task by ID | None |
 | PUT | `/tasks/:id` | Update a task | `{ "title": "Buy milk", "done": true }` |
 | DELETE | `/tasks/:id` | Delete a task | None |

 Task IDs are numeric. The PUT endpoint preserves fields that are omitted from
 the request body.

 ## Example response

 Command:

 ```bash
 curl -i http://localhost:3000/tasks
 ```

 Output:

 ```text
 HTTP/1.1 200 OK
 X-Powered-By: Express
 Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
 Content-Length: 129
 
 [{"id":0,"title":"Do laundry","done":false},{"id":1,"title":"Cook rice","done":false},{"id":2,"title":"Take a bath","done":true}]
 ```

